@@ -12,6 +12,14 @@ pip install runanywhere==0.20.11
 
 Wheels bundle the compiled native runtime and dependent libraries on Windows, macOS, and Linux. Python **3.9+** and `numpy >= 1.21` are required.
 
+> **Building from source (Linux).** If no wheel is available for your platform yet, build from
+> this directory: `pip install 'grpcio-tools==1.71.*'` (plus `protoc` on PATH), run
+> `./idl/codegen/generate_all.sh --only python` from the repo root, then `pip install .`.
+> A plain local build is not repaired by `auditwheel`, so `libonnxruntime.so.1` is not placed
+> next to `_core`; build with `-C build-dir=build/py` and run
+> `python scripts/bundle_native.py build/py` (or copy the ONNX Runtime library the build
+> downloaded into `runanywhere/_native/`) before `import runanywhere`.
+
